      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "After presenting five individual cases, the authors confirm the possibility of a diagnosis of sudden cardiac death where myocardial and/or coronary arteries lesions were present, by performing an exhumed body's autopsy even after a considerable amount of time after death. With regard to this procedure, performed only by experienced consultants specializing, a particularly accurate verification is necessary."},
